module main

import stdlib.repl
import stdlib.compiler.source as source

# The one golden-corpus program that bundles the SELF-HOSTED COMPILER.
#
# Every other corpus entry is a user-level program, so its IR moves only when
# codegen for user constructs moves. This one pulls `stdlib.compiler.*` in
# transitively through `stdlib.repl`, which makes its golden the only place a
# change to the compiler's OWN internals shows up as an IR diff — ~80k lines of
# it. That is load-bearing coverage, not incidental bulk: it is what noticed the
# `SourcePos` ADT→record conversion (the tag dispatch a single-constructor match
# was paying, and SourcePos's now-absent `sprout_register_ctor`), neither of which
# any user-level example can see.
#
# It replaces `examples/repl_hosted.sprout`, which held this role until it was
# removed. Two things improved in the move:
#
#   - `tests/smoke_shapes/` is covered by `just smoke-shapes` (DoD #7 — the
#     `str_concat(ptr null,…)` null-pointer codegen guard). `examples/` is not,
#     so the compiler-bundling shape was previously outside that check.
#   - A smoke shape is IR-only — never linked, never run — which suits a program
#     whose `main` is an interactive REPL loop far better than an `examples/`
#     entry did (examples are compiled, and five of them are run by
#     `just run-example-canary`).
#
# `repl.run()` is CALLED rather than merely imported: an unreferenced import
# gives the bundler license to emit none of the module, and the whole point here
# is that the compiler's code reaches the IR.
#
# `stdlib.compiler.source` is imported DIRECTLY, and used, on purpose. The
# transitive path through `stdlib.repl` is what supplies the breadth, but it is
# also invisible — were `repl` ever refactored to stop reaching the compiler,
# this file would still compile and the coverage would vanish silently. The
# direct dependency anchors the intent where a reader (and a grep) can see it.

fn origin_line() -> Int =
  source.source_position(source.cursor_from_string("")).line

fn main() -> Unit !{IO} =
  if origin_line() == 1 then repl.run() else print(origin_line())
